//
// An out-of-order channel takes the objects its queue was pushed for and
// stops, so the receiving core pushes again as it goes. The design in test.py
// moves more objects than one push covers, so without those pushes the core
// waits forever on an object the channel never takes.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, xrt_python_bindings
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test.py
//
// The wait for room on the queue is what costs; the run reports its time
// either way.
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% env CHECK_QUEUE_SPACE=0 %python %S/test.py
